https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WH4pBwR-rfA   (Capo 1) (MC1)

Phil wrote this with two key changes which makes the bridge a little messy.  Afterwards is another version that keeps common chords but requires a capo change.

TIP:  For the intro it's covered 5th string <c>, strum (C); covered top string <g>, strum (G).  Repeat.  (Notes may or may not transpose.)

TIP:  (F4) is actually (G#) but play it as an F-shape on the 4th fret.

TIP:  The “lilt” is 6 notes that can be easily plucked without any chords.  The notes are:  (all 1st string) 3rd fret <g>, 5th fret <a>, 3rd fret <g>, 1st fret <f>, 1st string open <e>; and then 3rd fret/2nd string <d>.  If you don't want to pick the lilt then play a (G) instead. 


